A request-logging module stores the request ID with AsyncLocalStorage. Listeners for a shared EventEmitter are registered while handling request 1, and the event is emitted later while handling request 2. What do the listeners see?

```js
als.run("req-1", () => {
  bus.on('done', () => log(als.getStore()));
  bus.on('done', AsyncResource.bind(() => log(als.getStore())));
});
als.run("req-2", () => setTimeout(() => bus.emit('done'), 0));
```
